*** Resetting replication at the very beginning of the test.

*** Generating a configuration file in JSON format for the Binlog
*** Server utility.

*** Determining binlog file directory from the server.

*** Creating a temporary directory <BINSRV_STORAGE_PATH> for storing
*** binlog files downloaded via the Binlog Server utility.

*** Creating a simple table and filling it with some data.
CREATE TABLE t1(id INT UNSIGNED NOT NULL PRIMARY KEY) ENGINE=InnoDB;
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(1);

*** Flushing the first binary log and switching to the second one.
FLUSH BINARY LOGS;

*** Filling the table with more data.
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(2);

*** Purging the first binary log.
PURGE BINARY LOGS TO '<second_binlog>';
include/assert.inc [gtid_purged must contain the first two transactions]

*** Shutting down the upstream MySQL server so PBS cannot pull
*** anything and the storage stays empty while the downstream
*** replica connects.

*** Starting Binlog Server Utility in background in pull mode.

*** Waiting for the replication source listener port ready to accept
*** connections.

*** Requesting non-blocking dumps while the storage is still empty.
*** GTID-based and position-based ones without the binlog file name
*** to start from must simply get EOF ('mysqlbinlog' exits with a
*** non-zero status if the connection is lost instead).

*** GTID-based and position-based dumps with the binlog file name to
*** start from must be rejected as this binlog file does not exist (yet).
Could not find first log file name in binary log index file
Could not find first log file name in binary log index file

*** Restarting the Binlog Server Utility (the storage is still empty) so
*** that its fresh log contains records only of the blocking dump session
*** below.

*** Starting a blocking downstream mysqlbinlog session requesting a
*** GTID-based dump with an empty GTID set.

*** Waiting for PBS's log to record that the sender reached the
*** empty-storage polling path (the purged GTIDs check is postponed
*** until the storage becomes non-empty).
include/wait_for_pattern_in_file.inc [sender : waiting for first binlog in empty storage]

*** Verifying the downstream mysqlbinlog session is still alive
*** while PBS has nothing in storage.

*** Starting the upstream MySQL server again. PBS's collector
*** thread will notice on its next iteration (idle_time=1s), take
*** the upstream's gtid_purged as the purged GTIDs of the storage
*** and start populating it.
# restart

*** Waiting for the downstream mysqlbinlog session to be rejected
*** (with the GTID set sent by the replica and the missing GTIDs
*** reported in the error message).
include/wait_for_pattern_in_file.inc [Cannot replicate because the source purged required binary logs.* The GTID set sent by the replica is '', and the missing transactions are '[-0-9a-f]+:1-2']

*** Waiting for the downstream mysqlbinlog session to terminate.

*** Sending SIGTERM signal to the Binlog Server Utility and waiting
*** for the process to terminate.

*** Filling the table with more data (so that the binary log created
*** by the MySQL Server restart is not empty).
INSERT INTO t1 VALUES(3);

*** Fetching the rest of the binary logs to make sure that the storage
*** is fully synchronized with the upstream MySQL server.

*** Starting Binlog Server Utility in background in pull mode once
*** again (now with a non-empty storage).

*** Waiting for the replication source listener port ready to accept
*** connections.

*** Requesting a GTID-based dump with an empty GTID set (none of the
*** purged GTIDs is executed by the replica). Expecting an error.
Cannot replicate because the source purged required binary logs. Replicate the missing transactions from elsewhere, or provision a new replica from backup. Consider increasing the source's binary log expiration period. The GTID set sent by the replica is '', and the missing transactions are '<server_uuid>:1-2'

*** Requesting a GTID-based dump with a GTID set that includes only
*** some of the purged GTIDs. Expecting an error.
Cannot replicate because the source purged required binary logs. Replicate the missing transactions from elsewhere, or provision a new replica from backup. Consider increasing the source's binary log expiration period. The GTID set sent by the replica is '<server_uuid>:1', and the missing transactions are '<server_uuid>:2'

*** Requesting a GTID-based dump that names a start binlog file with
*** an empty GTID set. Similarly to MySQL Server, no GTID-related checks
*** are performed in this case. Expecting the same events as from the
*** MySQL Server.

*** Comparing event sequences from the PBS and MySQL Server starting
*** from checkpoint 'from the named binlog file with the empty GTID set'.

*** Checking that the Binlog Server Utility received the start binlog
*** file name in the GTID-based dump request.
include/assert_grep.inc [GTID-based dump must start from the named binlog file]

*** Requesting GTID-based (with a GTID set that includes all the purged
*** GTIDs) and position-based dumps that name a non-existent start binlog
*** file. Expecting an error.
Could not find first log file name in binary log index file
Could not find first log file name in binary log index file

*** Requesting a GTID-based dump with a GTID set that includes all the
*** purged GTIDs. Expecting the same events as from the MySQL Server.

*** Comparing event sequences from the PBS and MySQL Server starting
*** from checkpoint 'from the purged GTID set'.

*** Checking that the rejections were logged by the Binlog Server
*** Utility.
include/assert_grep.inc [rejections must be logged by the Binlog Server Utility]

*** Sending SIGTERM signal to the Binlog Server Utility and waiting for
*** the process to terminate.

*** Dropping the table.
DROP TABLE t1;

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility storage directory.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility log file.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility configuration file.
